## As a user I want to view real time weather data for my city so that I can plan my day.

## Spec-driven development
# Spec Kit generates requirements, a plan, and tasks to guide a coding agent through an iterative, structured development process.
# i use this repo https://github.com/owainow/speckit-to-issue/tree/main, as a tool that converts Spec Kit outputs into GitHub issues.
# Idea → Spec → Tasks → GitHub Issues → Implementation

# 1. Clone and install the tool
git clone https://github.com/owainow/speckit-to-issue.git
cd speckit-to-issue

# Create a virtual environment
python -m venv venv
venv\Scripts\activate

# Quick helper: create new spec from a one-line prompt
# From the repository root run (Windows):
#
# promptkit.specify.bat "Add 5-day forecast feature"
#
# This creates `specs/<slug>.md` which you can convert into GitHub issues with:
#
# npm run generate-issues -- specs/<slug>.md

# 2. Create or obtain a Spec Kit spec
/specs/weather-app.md

# 3. prompt
/promptkit.specify "Build a weather app using OpenWeather API"

# 4. Convert spec into GitHub issues
npm run generate-issues -- path/to/spec.md

# 5. Add new features using new specs
/promptkit.specify "Add 5-day forecast feature" 

